    "problem_statement": "Server state machine not processing client requests properly\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen processing HTTP requests, the server connection state is not properly updated to handle incoming client requests. The server state machine appears to be missing critical transitions that should occur when a client sends a Request event.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport h11\n\n# Create a server connection\nconn = h11.Connection(h11.SERVER)\n\n# Simulate receiving a basic HTTP request\nrequest_data = b'GET / HTTP/1.1\\r\\nHost: example.com\\r\\n\\r\\n'\nconn.receive_data(request_data)\n\n# Try to get the request event\nevent = conn.next_event()\nprint(f\"Event type: {type(event)}\")\nprint(f\"Server state: {conn.our_state}\")\nprint(f\"Client state: {conn.their_state}\")\n\n# Expected: Server should be in SEND_RESPONSE state after processing Request\n# Actual: Server remains in incorrect state\n```\n\nThe issue becomes more apparent when trying to handle pipelined requests or when the server needs to process multiple request/response cycles. The connection state machine doesn't properly transition the server state when client Request events are processed.\n\nThis affects basic HTTP server functionality where the server should move to SEND_RESPONSE state after receiving and processing a client request."
